# rota accounts file: the roster of seats this machine may launch on.
#
# Install at ~/.config/claude-failover/accounts (or wherever CLAUDE_FAILOVER_HOME
# points), one seat per line:
#
#     <label>|<config_dir>
#
#   label       the email the seat is logged in as. It is what `rota usage`,
#               `rota switch` and the accounts map key on, and `rota reconcile`
#               rewrites it from the dir's own identity if the two ever drift.
#   config_dir  the CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR that seat lives in. One dir per seat,
#               under one pool root, with no spaces anywhere in the path. The
#               dir's basename is the alias you type: `rota switch work`.
#
# Order matters: put the seat whose weekly window resets SOONEST first, so its
# headroom is spent before it expires. Lines starting with # and blank lines
# are ignored. `rota pool-init` creates every dir listed here (and the shared
# settings/transcript links inside it) but never touches a credential; each
# seat is logged in once with `rota login <alias>`.
#
# Replace the emails below with the seats you own and pay for. Two or three
# rows is typical; the tool has no upper limit.

personal@example.com|~/.claude-pool/personal
work@example.com|~/.claude-pool/work
team@example.com|~/.claude-pool/team
